From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:44:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: BCM5301X: EA6900: add port 5 for the flow accelerator traps

Describe switch port 5, connected to gmac0, as a second CPU port. b53
redirects the frames that the flow accelerator in front of port 8
cannot handle (TTL 1, TCP FIN and RST) to it. The tree has one tagger,
so the port names the same one as port 8; it carries the regular tag.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4708-linksys-ea6900.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4708-linksys-ea6900.dts
@@ -139,7 +139,16 @@
 		};
 
 		port@5 {
-			status = "disabled";
+			/* takes the flow accelerator's traps, see b53_common.c;
+			 * one tagger per tree, and this port carries the
+			 * regular tag
+			 */
+			dsa-tag-protocol = "brcm-prepend";
+
+			fixed-link {
+				speed = <1000>;
+				full-duplex;
+			};
 		};
 
 		port@7 {
